Death & Taxes Bot — release version

This file is auto-stamped when the code is downloaded as a ZIP/tarball from GitHub
(the "Download ZIP" button, or a tag/release archive). The placeholders below are
replaced by `git archive` via .gitattributes `export-subst`:

  Version: $Format:%(describe:tags)$
  Commit:  $Format:%H$
  Date:    $Format:%cI$

Notes:
  - Downloaded from a tag (e.g. v1.0.0)  -> Version reads "v1.0.0".
  - Downloaded from the master branch    -> Version reads "v1.0.0-<n>-g<sha>"
    (the latest release plus how many commits past it you are).
  - In a plain `git clone` these stay as raw, unsubstituted placeholders, because
    substitution only happens at archive time. In that case, check the "version"
    field in package.json, the VERSION constant in
    packages/shared/src/constants.ts, or run `git describe --tags`.
  - DO NOT commit substituted values here. Doing so freezes the file at whatever
    version was current then, and every later archive reports that stale version —
    which is exactly what happened between v0.5.0 and v1.0.0. The updater reads
    constants.ts instead, precisely because this file could not be trusted.
